SUMMARY:Choose Between a 5 KM/3.1 Mile and a 10 KM/6.2 Mile Guided Waynesv
 ille Walk
DESCRIPTION:Haywood County Walking Meetup Group\nWe will be joining the As
 heville Amblers\, AARP\, the Cardinals Elite Walking Team\, and perhaps so
 me others for this event. Registration is at 9:30 a.m. with step-off at 10
 :00. The walk is free\, although the Amblers do accept donations (suggeste
 d donation $4.00).\n\nMeet in front of Mast General Store\, 63 N. Main St.
 \, Waynesville NC 28786. The walks go past public art\, Civil War sites\, 
 along the Waynesville Greenway\, and more. The 10 KM walk adds Town Hall\,
  the historic Frog Level area\, nice neighborhoods\, and a peaceful cemete
 ry with spectacular views.\n\nNote: the 5 KM walk will be at a slightly sl
 ower pace. The 10 KM walk will be at a slightly faster pace.\n\nThere are 
 some hills\, so some may want walking poles (I will be taking both of mine
 )\; sneakers should be fine. Dogs are welcome. Strollers should be ok\, th
 ough it will require one or two work-arounds. Bring plenty of water and a 
 protein snack. Dress appropriately for the weather.\n\nParking is easier a
  block to either side of Main Street. Mast General Store doesn't have a pu
 blic restroom\, but we can direct you to one nearby should you need it.\n\
 nMany people go out to eat together after this walk at places like Sweet O
 nion and Angelos. You will want to shop at Mast General Store and several 
 other downtown shops. The last time we did this walk\, people were asking 
 about the availability of ice cream and chocolates.\n\nWhy not make a day 
 of it!
