SUMMARY:See the Sights of Cherokee on a 10 KM/6.2 mile Walk
DESCRIPTION:Haywood County Walking Meetup Group\nWe'll gather at the Welco
 me Center across from the fairgrounds. Our route takes us past the Museum 
 of the Cherokee People and the Qualla Arts and Crafts facility. We then wa
 lk the road up to the *Unto These Hills* Amphitheatre. From there we pass 
 the Oconaluftee Indian Village and walk through the Botanical Gardens. Com
 ing back down the back way\, we loop around ending up at the Oconaluftee I
 slands Park with its "bamboo forest." From there we return to the start po
 int.\n\nHiking boots are not needed\, though some will want walking poles.
  (I plan to take both of mine.) Do bring plenty of water and a protein sna
 ck. Dress for the weather. I'm not sure whether dogs are allowed in the Bo
 tanical Gardens\, but it is a short loop and if necessary\, you can walk a
 round the parking lot for the few minutes it will take us to make that loo
 p. While much of this walk is on pavement\, trail strollers would be neede
 d for the walk\, with a few workarounds.\n\nDrive into Cherokee on US-441.
  When you pass the Cherokee movie theater\, the highway will turn left. Lo
 ok for the fairgrounds on your left and the Welcome Center on your right. 
 We will gather in the parking lot. There are restrooms in the Welcome Cent
 er.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/haywood-county-walking-meetup-group/e
 vents/316727471/
