SUMMARY:Walking the NC Arboretum at the Willow Pond & Old Mill Trail
DESCRIPTION:Haywood County Walking Meetup Group\nMeet inside the Baker Vis
 itor Center. Restrooms are available at the start point. We will start wal
 king as soon as everyone has arrived.\n\nThe walk is a guided 5 KM trail. 
 There are some moderate hills and stair climbing. A significant part of th
 e route is on well-groomed trails with very few obstacles. Some people wil
 l want walking poles.\n\nAfter exploring the Formal Gardens (Winter Lights
  will be up!)\, we will walk down Running Cedar Road and turn left on Bent
  Creek Road. We'll turn right on the Old Mill Trail and go out and back. T
 hen we will take the Wesley Branch Trail and go right on the Lower Willow 
 Pond Trail. After exploring the Willow Pond\, we will follow the Upper Wil
 low Pond Trail to the parking lot.\n\nDress for the weather\; consider a h
 at and sunscreen (yes\, even in December). Sneakers should be fine\, unles
 s it has rained recently. Be sure to bring **plenty of water** and a prote
 in snack.\n\nDogs on leash are welcome but are not allowed in buildings or
  in the Bonsai Exhibit. Trail strollers should be ok.\n\nThe NC Arboretum 
 does not have an admission fee\, but they charge $25 per car parking fee (
 so pack as many people in your car as you can). We recommend the driver pu
 rchase the lowest level annual membership which includes free parking. (Of
  course\, you may want a higher-level membership\, your choice.) We walk a
 t the Arboretum at least six times per year. A third option is to go to th
 e comments section of this page and ask whether anyone would be willing to
  meet you and drive you into the Arboretum.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/haywood-county-walking-meetup-group/e
 vents/317385174/
