SUMMARY:Walk 10 KM on the Pickens Doodle Trail from Pickens SC
DESCRIPTION:Haywood County Walking Meetup Group\nThe Pickens SC trailhead 
 for the Doodle Trail is at 409 E. Cedar Rock Street\, Pickens SC 29671. Th
 e trail is a 7.5 mile rails-to-trails partnership between the City of Easl
 ey and the City of Pickens. We will be start at the Pickens trailhead\, wa
 lk 3 miles\, and return to the start point. We will be sharing the trail w
 ith bikers\, runners\, and rollerbladers.\n\nLocal residents nicknamed the
  railroad the "Pickens Doodle" line\, because the freight engine could not
  be turned around and had to run backwards from Easley to Pickens\, lookin
 g like a doodlebug.\n\nPickens Doodle Park\, where the trailhead is locate
 d\, includes restroom facilities\, a railroad depot museum\, a pavilion\, 
 benches\, bike racks\, and a train-themed playground.\n\nDress for the wea
 ther. You probably won't need a walking stick (although I plan to take one
 ). Bring plenty of water and a protein snack. Consider a hat and sunscreen
  (yes\, even though it is December). Wheelchairs and strollers should have
  no problem. Dogs are welcome (though you must clean up after your pet).\n
 \nThis is a new walk for me. Come and help me explore an interesting new l
 ocation.
